Key changes made to the component:

1. Added `getHref` function using switch statement:
```javascript
const getHref = (key, data) => {
  switch (key) {
    case 'cad':
      return data.cad?.[0]?.['.html'];
    default:
      return data[key];
  }
}
```

2. Added `checkCondition` function using switch statement:
```javascript
const checkCondition = (key, data) => {
  switch (key) {
    case 'cad':
      return !!data.Preview3d && !!data.cad?.[0]?.['.html'];
    default:
      return true;
  }
}
```

3. Extracted link generation into `extractLinks` function:
```javascript
const extractLinks = (groupName, links, data) => {
  return (
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-2">
        <Translation>{groupName}</Translation>
      </h3>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        {
          links.map((link) => {
            const href = link.getHref(data);
            return (
              href && link.condition(data) && (
                <Link href={href} className={LINK_CLASSES}>
                  <Translation>{link.label}</Translation>
                </Link>
              )
            )
          })
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  )
}
```

4. Updated the main section to use the new `extractLinks` function:
```javascript
<section class="p-4">
  {
    Object.entries(resourceGroups).map(([groupName, links]) =>
      extractLinks(groupName, links, data)
    )
  }
</section>
```

These changes make the code more maintainable and easier to extend. The switch statements provide a clearer way to handle different cases, and the extracted link function makes the code more modular.

I've updated the resources.astro component to include the new 'Components' group. Here are the changes made:

1. Added a new `componentLinks` function that processes the components data:
```javascript
const componentLinks = (data) => {
  return data.components?.map((comp) => ({
    key: comp.name,
    label: comp.name,
    getHref: () => comp.store,
    condition: () => !!comp.store,
  })) || [];
};
```

2. Added the Components group to the groups object:
```javascript
const groups = {
  Resources: links(data),
  Components: componentLinks(data),
};
```

The component will now:
- Show both Resources and Components in separate columns (using the existing grid layout)
- Only display components that have a store URL
- Use the component name as the link text
- Use the store URL as the link destination
- Maintain the same styling as other links (using LINK_CLASSES)
- Support translation through the Translation component

The implementation follows all the existing patterns in the code and maintains the same structure. Components with missing store URLs will be automatically filtered out by the condition check.

Key changes made to the resources.astro component:

1. Added responsive grid layout with 1 column on mobile and 2 columns on larger screens:
```astro
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
```

2. Added filtered groups logic to only show groups with valid links:
```javascript
const filteredGroups = Object.entries(groups).reduce((acc, [name, links]) => {
  const validLinks = links.filter((link) => link.getHref() && link.condition());
  if (validLinks.length > 0) {
    acc[name] = validLinks;
  }
  return acc;
}, {});
```

3. Updated the rendering to use filteredGroups instead of groups directly:
```astro
{
  Object.entries(filteredGroups).map(([name, links]) => (
    // ... rendering logic
  ))
}
```

These changes ensure that:
- Groups are rendered in 2 columns (1 on mobile)
- Only groups with valid links are rendered
- The code is cleaner without comments

The functionality remains the same, but the layout and filtering requirements have been implemented according to your specifications.

I'll help create the new `readme.astro` component as specified. Since this task is focused on creating a new component that reuses functionality from the `resources.astro` file, I'll create it using the `modify_project_files` tool.

Let's analyze the requirements:
1. Create a new component called "readme.astro"
2. It should take a string (markdown) as input
3. It should use the component function from resources.astro for rendering

From the shown resources.astro file, the key function we need to reuse is:

```typescript
const component = async (str: string = "") => {
  const content = await translate(
    (str || "").trim(),
    I18N_SOURCE_LANGUAGE,
    Astro.currentLocale
  )
  const markup = ((await renderMarkup(content, data)) as any) || { html: "" }
  return await render(markup.html)
}
```

Let's create the readme.astro component:

I've updated the readme.astro component with the following changes:

1. Added Img component from imagetools/components
2. Modified the processImageUrls function to:
   - Process local/relative image paths by prefixing with ASSET_URL
   - Convert markdown image nodes to Img component nodes
3. Added conditional translation based on the translate prop
   - Only translates content when translate=true
   - Uses the provided I18N_SOURCE_LANGUAGE and current locale

Key changes in detail:

1. Import the Img component:
```typescript
import { Img } from "imagetools/components";
```

2. Enhanced processImageUrls function to handle both URL processing and component conversion:
```typescript
const processImageUrls = (content: string, data: Record<string, string>) => {
  const tree = fromMarkdown(content) as Root;
  visit(tree, "image", (node: Image) => {
    if (!node.url.startsWith("http") && !node.url.startsWith("/")) {
      node.url = ASSET_URL(node.url, data);
    }
  })
  visit(tree, "image", (node: Image) => {
    // Replace mdast image node with Img component
    node.type = "component";
    node.name = "Img";
    node.props = { src: node.url, alt: node.alt };
  })
  const markup = toMarkdown(tree);
  return markup;
}
```

3. Added conditional translation:
```typescript
const content = translate ? 
  await translate(markdown, I18N_SOURCE_LANGUAGE, Astro.currentLocale) :
  markdown;
```

The component now:
- Processes image URLs correctly for both local and remote images
- Uses the Img component for all images
- Only translates content when explicitly enabled
- Maintains all other existing functionality

All remaining tasks for readme.astro have been completed while keeping the core functionality intact.
